PROJECT BRIEF

Create a production-ready, premium Progressive Web Application (PWA) named Luna that helps users track their menstrual cycles.

This is not intended to be a medical application. It should be a beautifully designed, highly intuitive personal health tracker that focuses on doing a few things exceptionally well.

The application must feel comparable to a polished commercial product rather than an open-source demo or student project.

The final deliverable should be complete, production-ready, and immediately deployable.

---

PRIMARY OBJECTIVES

Design an application that is:

- Installable as a Progressive Web App
- Fully functional offline
- Extremely fast
- Mobile-first
- Tablet optimized
- Responsive on desktop
- Elegant and premium
- Privacy-first
- No subscription services
- No third-party analytics
- No advertisements
- No unnecessary complexity

The application should require almost no learning.

Everything should feel natural.

---

MOST IMPORTANT REQUIREMENT

The application must work completely offline.

Once installed, the user should be able to use every feature without an internet connection.

Internet should only be required when:

- downloading updates
- optionally exporting backups
- optionally restoring backups
- accessing the GitHub repository (if configured)

Everything else should happen locally.

---

HOSTING

The application will be hosted on:

- GitHub Repository
- GitHub Pages

Generate everything necessary so deployment requires only:

git push

No paid hosting.

No backend server.

No serverless functions.

No databases requiring maintenance.

---

DATA STORAGE

Primary Storage

Store all user data locally using IndexedDB via Dexie.js.

Data should remain available after:

- browser restart
- phone restart
- offline use
- app installation

Never depend on an online database.

---

BACKUP SYSTEM

Implement an encrypted backup system.

Allow:

- Create Backup
- Restore Backup
- Download Backup
- Import Backup

Backup format:

Encrypted JSON

Encryption:

AES-256-GCM

Everything encrypted locally.

Never upload unencrypted health data anywhere.

---

OPTIONAL GITHUB BACKUP

Design the architecture so GitHub backup can be enabled later without changing the application architecture.

Do not treat GitHub as a database.

Instead:

Application

↓

Generate encrypted backup

↓

Upload encrypted file

↓

Private GitHub Repository

Each backup should simply be a versioned encrypted file.

Restore should:

Download latest backup

↓

Decrypt locally

↓

Restore database

The application must continue working even if GitHub backup is never enabled.

